/* Smoke: bring the window up at a fixed size, let it settle, and print it.

   A script body is ONLY the statements of run() - no imports, no class, and it
   may name no type at all.  Everything below is inherited from
   AbstractAutomationScript.

   The screenshot path is RELATIVE on purpose: the engine starts this JVM with
   the scenario directory as its working directory, so the file lands beside
   this script and nowhere near the developer's own files.  The image, not the
   check, is the real evidence here - the test asserts it is a genuine PNG. */
sizeMainWindow(1366, 768);
waitSeconds(1);
screenshot("multifunctional", "smoke.png");
checkTrue("window-up", true);
